  "body": "Section 12.1.2.3 specifies that an attribute value may be composed only of text and character references and may not include an ambiguous ampersand, but I did not find an applicable definition of \"text\" in the HTML Living Standard or linked to from the Standard. The word is linked from but the link is not to a definition. There should be one.\r\n\r\nI tried searching the whole spec for a definition, either inline or linked to, but my browser says there are more than 1,000 instances of the string even when the Whole Words option is selected. I looked at the earliest instances in the spec and in what I thought would be the likeliest sections, but didn't see the definition. If it's elsewhere in the spec, please put it in a likely section.\r\n\r\nIt now obviously allows more than alphanumerics or 12.1.2.3 would have said that instead of \"text\". Since an attribute value could be for the href attribute and in that case has to be a URL, text would have to include any character allowed in a URL (such as \":\", \"/\", \"#\", and \"?\").\r\n\r\nI do not know enough to propose a definition.",
